1
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:05,800
有消息了吗
Do we know anything?

2
00:00:06,284 --> 00:00:07,594
没 医生正在里面诊断
No. They're in there now with the doctor.

3
00:00:07,594 --> 00:00:08,364
不过已经是万幸了
We're lucky though.

4
00:00:08,364 --> 00:00:10,504
急救员说完全有可能比现在的情况严重的多
The paramedics said it could have been a lot worse.

5
00:00:10,574 --> 00:00:12,324
老天 怎么会发生这种事
My God, how did this even happen?

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,380
儿子来了 大日子快到了哦
There he is. Big day's coming up.

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:18,920
你生日想要什么样的礼物 小狗娃
What do you want for your birthday, big dog?

8
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,160
没事的 我不想要
It's okay. I'm good.

9
00:00:20,544 --> 00:00:23,334
来嘛 除了上天什么都行
Come on. Sky's the limit.

10
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:24,780
狮子大开口吧 儿子
Dream big, my boy.

11
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:27,580
-我觉得送我一条皮带挺好的 -皮带
- Well, I guess I could use a belt. - A belt?

12
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,780
是啊 你说的对 我根本不需要
Yeah, you're right. I don't need it.

13
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,220
天线延长线用着也挺顺手的
Extension cord works pretty good.

14
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,920
每年卢克的生日都在感恩节附近
Every year, Luke's birthday falls right around Thanksgiving,

15
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:39,780
所以大家都忙着准备过节了
and so it gets lost in the holiday shuffle.

16
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,240
有一年我们彻底忘到九霄云外了
One year we forgot completely,

17
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,140
只好用火鸡填料临时做了个蛋糕
and we had to improvise a cake of stuffing.

18
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,640
说一下 他一点都不介意
Which, by the way, he was fine with.

19
00:00:44,655 --> 00:00:45,255
他是那种古怪孩子
He's one of those kids,

20
00:00:45,255 --> 00:00:47,595
你送他一份礼物 他却只想着玩盒子
you get him a gift and all he wants to do is play with the box.

21
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,720
是啊 有一年我们直接送他一个盒子
Yeah, one year we actually just got him a box,

22
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,200
一个非常漂亮的盒子
a really nice box.

23
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:53,600
但我们犯了个错 将之放进了礼品袋
And we made the mistake of putting it in a gift bag.

24
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,520
所以他就玩起了礼品袋
So he played with the gift bag.

25
00:00:56,665 --> 00:00:58,025
-我们怎么都做不对 -做不对
- We can't get it right. - No.

26
00:00:58,025 --> 00:01:01,305
-我觉得很愧疚 我们得做点什么 -是啊
- I feel terrible. We gotta do something. - Oh, yeah.

27
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,240
话说 家人们准备趁感恩节来个
You know, the family is gonna be together for Thanksgiving...

28
00:01:04,415 --> 00:01:06,355
大团圆聚会 我不知道会持续多久
for the first time in I don't even know how long.

29
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,960
我太同意你了 我们应该取消聚会
I am so with you. We should blow this out...

30
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,960
给卢克办一个有史以来最棒的生日派对
and throw Luke the best birthday party of all time.

31
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:11,900
对 对 我们可以订购许多匹萨
Yes. Yes. And we'll order a whole bunch of pizzas...

32
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,080
设立一个手工艺品桌
and set up an arts and crafts table.

33
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:16,120
-什么 -手工艺品桌
- A what? - A crafts table.

34
00:01:16,155 --> 00:01:17,955
就是 大家都围在一起
You know, where everybody gathers around

35
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:20,680
他们就发现了自己最爱的派对项目
They got their own party favor.

36
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,140
抱歉 我睡着了
Sorry. I fell asleep

37
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,100
你说的简直是史上最无聊的派对
while you were describing the most boring party ever.

38
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:42,240
-几小时后再见了 -好的
- See you in a few hours. - Yeah.

39
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,760
再次谢谢你们借我卡拉OK唱机
Thanks again for the karaoke machine.

40
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,220
派对办完后 我会立刻送过来的
I'll get it back to you right after the party.

41
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:46,000
那再好不过了
That'd be great.

42
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,000
千万不要 求你了
Please don't. I beg you.

43
00:01:48,096 --> 00:01:49,566
-千万别送回来 -好的
- Don't bring it back. - Okay.

44
00:01:49,566 --> 00:01:52,026
嘿 菲尔 你今天的派对有请小丑吗
Hey, Phil. Are, uh, you getting a clown for today?

45
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:55,620
没 卢克不怎么喜欢小丑
Oh, no. Luke's not much of a clown fan.

46
00:01:56,806 --> 00:01:58,447
-真的吗 -是啊 他从来不喜欢小丑
- Really? - Yeah. He never liked 'em.

47
00:01:58,600 --> 00:01:59,760
他有见过出色的小丑吗
Has he ever seen a good one?

48
00:02:00,446 --> 00:02:02,406
有谁 见过吗
Has- Has anyone?

49
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,740
真的 总之 谢谢你们了
Really. So anyway, thanks again.

50
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,440
好的 一会儿见
Okay. See you later.

51
00:02:07,816 --> 00:02:10,746
-不要小丑 不要小丑吗 -算了吧
- No clown? No- No clown? - Let it go.

52
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:12,900
谁家开派对不请小丑
Who throws a party without a clown?

53
00:02:13,026 --> 00:02:15,177
从上世纪30年代开始 大部分人都不请了
Since the late '30s, I'd say most people.

54
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,540
话说 我们还没给卢克准备生日礼物
You know what? We haven't gotten Luke a present yet.

55
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,440
或许扮小丑可以当生日礼物
Maybe a clown could be our present.

56
00:02:19,567 --> 00:02:20,218
卡梅隆 卡梅隆
Cameron. Cameron.

57
00:02:20,287 --> 00:02:22,247
如果菲尔和克莱尔想给卢克请个小丑
If Phil and Claire wanted to get Luke a clown,

58
00:02:22,247 --> 00:02:24,117
他们肯定已经请了 那不是我们的派对
they would've. This is not our party.

59
00:02:24,117 --> 00:02:27,337
-但 -那不是我们家开派对
- But- - this is not our party.

60
00:02:27,337 --> 00:02:28,228
但我刚刚
But I just-

61
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:28,780
那好吧
Fine.

62
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:31,647
那你说我们送他什么礼物好
What would you suggest we get him then, hmm?

63
00:02:31,707 --> 00:02:33,197
送他一张礼物卡就行了
Get him a gift card.

64
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,640
-就礼物卡打发他吗 -是啊
- A gift card? - Yeah.

65
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,620
你被谁摧残过
Who hurt you?

66
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,380
嘿 歌洛莉亚
Hey, Gloria,

67
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:44,580
你知道怎么包装这玩意儿吗
you got any idea how to wrap one of these things?

68
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,500
-那是个十字弓吗 -是啊
- Is that a crossbow? - Yeah.

69
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:48,580
我是不是堪称世上最好的外公
Am I the greatest grandpa in the world or what?

70
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,440
我们不能送十字弓给卢克
We can't give Luke a crossbow.

71
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,620
他每次用吸管都能戳到眼睛
He pokes himself in the eye every time he uses a straw.

72
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,580
开什么玩笑 我像他那么大的时候就有一把
Are you kidding? I had one when I was his age.

73
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:58,140
我每射杀一只乌鸦 我爸就会给我25美分
My dad used to give me a quarter for every crow I bagged.

74
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,640
我曾经还有大砍刀呢
And I used to have a machete.

75
00:02:59,887 --> 00:03:01,798
-但时代已经变了 -他会没事的
- But times have changed. - He'll be fine.

76
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,680
我会教他怎么用的
I'll teach him how to use it.

77
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,200
嘿 老弟 过得怎么样
Hey, pal, how's it going?

78
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,080
我有魅力吗
Am I charming?

79
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:07,960
-靠 -你当然有魅力了
- Oh, boy. - Of course you're charming.

80
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,120
-谁说你没魅力了 -没人
- Who said you were not charming? - No one.

81
00:03:10,298 --> 00:03:12,768
学校里有个妹子挺好 我想让她喜欢我
But there's a girl in my school, and I want her to like me.

82
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,820
-我需要你的建议 杰 -真的吗
- I need your advice, Jay. - Really?

83
00:03:15,548 --> 00:03:17,418
她会去参加卢克的派对
She's gonna be at Luke's party.

84
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,220
我真是 有点受宠若惊
Well, I'm a little thrown.

85
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:22,200
我是说 你一般不会向我征询建议
I mean, you don't usually come to me for advice.

86
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,320
在泡美妞这方面 您老可算个中高手啊
Well, this is one area in which you've done pretty well.

87
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:26,920
他说的很对
He has a point.

88
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,880
我试过用各种方法吸引她的注意
I've tried everything to get her attention-

89
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:32,920
为她开门 在餐厅为她递上一杯牛奶
opening doors, having a milk sent over in the cafeteria.

90
00:03:33,188 --> 00:03:35,128
-全都不奏效 -事实上
- Nothing's worked. - Here's the deal.

91
00:03:35,188 --> 00:03:37,418
女孩子不吃浪漫那一套
Girls don't go for all that romantic stuff.

92
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,180
她们喜欢有权势的或成功的男人
They go for power and success.

93
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,040
既然这两样你都不沾边
And since you don't have either one of those things,

94
00:03:41,738 --> 00:03:43,399
那你就得做个风趣幽默的男人
you're gonna be the funny guy.

95
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:47,940
不不不 我想要你养的最危险的爬虫
No, no, no. I want the most dangerous reptile you've got.

96
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,340
我有一只吃蟋蟀的鼠鳞蜥
I have an iguana that eats crickets.

97
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,740
要是给蟋蟀办生日派对 那才算吓人吧
That'd be scary if it was a birthday party for crickets.

98
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,300
说真的 丛林女郎
Seriously, Jungle Tanya,

99
00:03:55,349 --> 00:03:56,819
我需要你升级一下恐怖程度
I need you step it up a notch.

100
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,880
有没有什么东西能把你自己吓个半死
Is there anything that scares the cocoa out of you?

101
00:03:59,049 --> 00:04:02,199
还真没有 不过我有条"胡须龙"[一种蜥蜴]
Uh, not really. I do have a bearded dragon.

102
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,660
-是吗 它会.. -不 它不会喷火
- Ooh. Does it- - No, it does not breathe fire.

103
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,120
那说来说去又说回去了 是吧
Well, then we're back to square one, aren't we?

104
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,920
我脑子里一直想着卢克的生日会
I couldn't get Luke out of my mind.

105
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,800
我知道我向米奇尔保证过
I know I made a promise to Mitchell,

106
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:17,740
但有些东西比"保证"二字要重要的多
but some things are bigger than promises.

107
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,880
菲茨宝一定要在派对上华丽登场
Fizbo would be at that party.

108
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,560
你好啊 老朋友
Hello, old friend.

109
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:35,360
一切都发生在眨眼之间
It all happened so fast.

110
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,020
我一直在想
I keep thinking

111
00:04:36,049 --> 00:04:37,170
我当时做点什么阻止这一切就好了
there was something I could've done.

112
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,380
不 你不要自责
No, don't blame yourself.

113
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,530
谁能想到会发生这种事呢
Who could've possibly seen it coming?

114
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:43,780
亲爱的 那是道攀岩墙 那安全吗
Sweetie, that's a rock wall. Is that even safe?

115
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,860
-老天啊 -亲爱的 放心
- Oh, my God. - Honey, relax.

116
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,780
嘿 有人因为这东西受过伤吗
Hey, has anyone ever gotten hurt on one of these things?

117
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:50,830
-我不知道 今天是我第一天上班 -瞧
- I don't know, man. It's my first day. - See?

118
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,710
他们肯让新人操作肯定说明没有...
They wouldn't let the new guy do it if it-

119
00:04:52,810 --> 00:04:54,670
-那只会让我更加担心 -别担心
- That did not make me feel better. - Don't worry.

120
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:56,750
我签了一堆的责任声明书
I signed, like, a hundred releases.

121
00:04:57,040 --> 00:05:00,260
我们什么时候决定弄这些的 太过了吧
When did we decide all this? I think it's too much.

122
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,480
瞧 我就知道你会这么说
See, I knew you'd say that.

123
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,460
所以我就没告诉你
That's why I didn't tell you.

124
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,320
所以你就放轻松 去吃个冰霜卷吧
So just relax. Grab a snow cone.

125
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,810
-你弄来了冰霜卷机器吗 -是啊
- There's a snow cone machine? - Yeah.

126
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:09,700
妈 记住 迪兰不能吃蛋黄酱
Mom, just so you know, Dylan cannot have mayonnaise.

127
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,730
没头没脑来这么一句 你干嘛告诉我这个
That's random. Why are you telling me that?

128
00:05:11,830 --> 00:05:14,520
-因为他要来参加派对 -有那个必要吗
- 'Cause he's coming to the party. - Is that absolutely necessary?

129
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:15,700
当然 因为她忍受不了10分钟
Yes, because she can't go 10

130
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,760
没有她男友的舌头在她嘴里搅
minutes without her boyfriend's tongue in her mouth.

131
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,620
就像他在喂幼鸟一样
It's like he's feeding a baby bird.

132
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:20,840
别羡慕嫉妒恨了
Don't be so jealous.

133
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,220
我确定你在计算机夏令营会遇到超级大帅哥的
I'm sure you'll meet someone super hot at computer camp.

134
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:25,871
-姑娘们 -嘿 别闹了
- Girls. - Hey. Hey.

135
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:26,960
你手上拿的什么
So, what you got there?

136
00:05:27,121 --> 00:05:28,622
是手工艺品桌需要的一些原材料
These are supplies for the crafts table.

137
00:05:28,681 --> 00:05:30,621
我终于想到我们要做什么了
I finally figured out what we're gonna be making.

138
00:05:30,691 --> 00:05:33,671
-让孩子们无聊吗 -我开玩笑的 玩笑
- Kids bored? - I'm teasing. I'm teasing.

139
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,300
看上去挺不错 是什么
It looks good. What is it?

140
00:05:36,041 --> 00:05:37,311
梳套
Comb sheaths.

141
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:39,040
我知道 我知道的
I know. I know.

142
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,740
但我是11岁的时候做的这个
But we made them when I was 11 years old

143
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,980
在唐娜·瑞格比的生日派对上
at Donna Rigby's birthday party.

144
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,480
一开始我们也觉得那很傻帽
At first we thought it was really stupid,

145
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,240
然后我们觉得那是很愉快的经历
and then we had a blast, so-

146
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,000
怎么可能不愉快呢
How could you not?

147
00:05:46,011 --> 00:05:48,641
你把孩子们最爱的两样东西结合到了一起
You combined the two things that kids love the most-

148
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,280
梳子和套子
combs and sheaths.

149
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:52,800
我开玩笑的
I'm kidding!

150
00:05:53,461 --> 00:05:55,401
我的梳子哪儿去了 噢
Where's my comb? Oh!

151
00:05:55,461 --> 00:05:59,071
原来在我超级方便的绣珠梳套里
Here it is in my incredibly convenient beaded comb sheath...

152
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:01,760
那可是我在卢克超棒的生日派对上做的哟
that I made at Luke's awesome birthday party.

153
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,240
一举夺魁 邓菲太太
Hole in one, Mrs. Dunphy.

154
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,300
一举夺魁
Hole in one.

155
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:07,040
我回家了
I'm home.

156
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:10,500
我给卢克买了一套游戏盘 但是关于数学的
I got Luke a video game, but it's about math.

157
00:06:10,641 --> 00:06:13,832
所以 我们估计是那种督促人学习的讨厌舅舅
So I guess we're those kind of uncles.

158
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:15,740
小卡
Cam.

159
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,020
别生气
Don't be mad.

160
00:06:22,702 --> 00:06:25,432
噢 小卡
Oh. Cam. Uh-

161
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,000
我立志想当小丑是从
I've known I wanted to be a clown...

162
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,260
我发现小丑不过是人化妆扮成的开始的
since I found out clowns were just people with makeup.

163
00:06:29,492 --> 00:06:32,222
实际上 当我成长为小少年的时候
Um, as a matter of fact, by the time I was a teenager,

164
00:06:32,292 --> 00:06:35,392
只要我不是在上学或钓鱼 就是在扮小丑
